[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/bonelight/ui/spells/ink-ring-dark.png" id="3_icon"]

; Ink Ring (scripts/InkRing.cs), 2026-11-09: Ma Liang's brush, walked. A thin line of ink trails the wizard; when his
; path crosses its own line the loop closes and everything inside is struck, then slowed for a moment. Water + Darkness,
; the two halves of the ink. Nobody's opener; everyone earns it with the Cormorant feat (Water and Darkness kills in one
; run). TargetingMode 8 is Drawn - his walk draws the area it strikes - and DamageShape 3 a burst over an area.
;
; NO TIMER PUTS ANYTHING INTO THE WORLD. BaseCooldown is the RECHARGE between rings: while it is ripe the fire loop arms
; the node, and a ring closes the moment his path crosses its line (Player.InkRing.cs). BaseDamage is ONE STRIKE of a
; ring on each body inside it. The ink's life is InkRing.BaseInkSeconds (2 s) plus the ZoneDuration lines here (Effect
; 13); the card says it as "Ink duration +20%", never in seconds. The slow (40% for 1.2 s) is the node's own.
;
; FIRST GUESSES, untuned. Spells start small (Eric, 2026-11-02): at level 1 the ink lasts 2 s, so at the wizard's walk
; only a ring about 140 units across can close before its start has dried; 3.6 s at level 8, about 250. Written out in
; full so Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of its own (ScalingTagsMask 8195: Damage, Cooldown, Duration):
; every level adds damage, even levels shorten the recharge by 0.1 s, odd ones and the last lengthen the ink by 0.4 s.
; Level 8: 30 a strike, a ring every 1.6 s at most, ink lasting 3.6 s.

